# Rows to merge into docs/TECH-DEBT.md

Source: Phase 2 (refactoring-patterns), pass on `play/src/front/Stores/MediaStore.ts` (2026-11-12). Baseline `HEAD` = `40f7184b1`, `MediaStore.ts` sha256 `fc5f6b6e…10403640d` (1,811 lines). After the four patches: `8dad9d1e…5b638470` (1,865 lines). Evidence: `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase2-mediastore/README.md`. Locations marked "after" are line numbers in the patched file; the others are `HEAD`'s.

## Debt Ledger: status updates

| Item | New status |
|---|---|
| MD-01 | Unchanged. The `OverconstrainedError` branch moved verbatim into `handleGetUserMediaFailure` (after `:787-800`). Still pinned by "MD-01 (pinned): a chosen camera the browser cannot open also drops the chosen microphone"; mutant R2 (Phase 1's M7 inside the new function) still fails it. |
| MD-02 | Unchanged. The stale-generation check stays in `runRawStreamUpdate`'s `try` (after `:1006-1011`); the queue is after `:1085-1118`. |
| MD-03 | Unchanged (fixed in `87b3c6e03`). The per-kind clears stay at the top of the run (after `:906-913`); the two writes moved verbatim into `handleGetUserMediaFailure` (camera after `:809-810`, microphone after `:822-823`). |
| MD-05 | Location update only: the comment is after `:1563-1571`, the three module-scope subscriptions after `:1711`, `:1729`, `:1803`. `04-correct-md05-comment.patch` corrects the comment so it says the chain runs from import, and that nothing is requested at import only because `myCameraStore` and `myMicrophoneStore` start `false`. The design row stays open: any input of `mediaStreamConstraintsStore` that starts `true` would still request a device at import. |

