| Long function with four error branches: `runRawStreamUpdate` (was 230 lines, `:776-1005`) | after `:868-1057` (`runRawStreamUpdate`, 190 lines), `:780-826` (`handleGetUserMediaFailure`, 47), `:832-839` (`TrackPlan`), `:845-866` (`planTracks`, 22) | partly done. `02-extract-getusermedia-failure-handler.patch` (Extract Function) moved the four error branches out of the `catch`. `03-extract-track-plan.patch` (Extract Function, the prescribed refactoring) made the stop and request decisions a pure function of the previous constraints, the new constraints and three track flags. Still in `runRawStreamUpdate`: the `navigator.mediaDevices` branches (a P3 gap, so not moved), the stop loops, the warm-track reuse, the request and the merge of the new tracks. The success path after `getUserMedia` (store writes, about 30 lines) is the next candidate. |

## Debt Ledger: new rows

None. Both new tests pin what the code does today, and neither branch showed a defect. One observation, not filed as a bug: a `NotReadableError` (camera taken by another application) records no access issue, because `MediaAccessIssue` has only `"permission_denied"` and `"no_device"`. The camera button then has no help context (`null`), while the first request's error (pinned: `rawLocalStreamStore` emits it) still reaches `MediaManager`, which shows the camera help popup when `myCameraStore` is `true` (`MediaManager.ts:35-39`; inferred from the code, not tested). Whether the tooltip should name this cause is a product call.
